        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "50√3 m",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "100 m",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Shortcut: Distance from tower base = Height × cot(angle). For 45°: d₁ = 50 × 1 = 50 m. For 30°: d₂ = 50 × √3 m. Distance between cars = d₂ - d₁ = 50(√3 - 1) m. Full: In right triangles, tan 45° = 50/x → x = 50. tan 30° = 50/y → y = 50√3. Required distance = y - x = 50√3 - 50 = 50(√3 - 1) m.",
